Article 20
The implementation of child and women protection is carried out through:  a. planning and development of child and women information systems;  b. prevention and protection;
c. child protection;
d. special protection;
e. women protection;
f. protection in the workplace;
g. handling and recovery of victims of violence;
h. rehabilitation, reintegration, and empowerment;
i. law enforcement services, and legal assistance; and  JDIH Kota Singkawang j. facilitation of juvenile justice.

Article 62
(1) For the prevention of acts of violence against women, the Regional Government shall conduct empowerment and awareness-raising to families and communities by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.
JDIH Kota Singkawang (2) In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows:
a. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
b. opening employment opportunities for women;
c. building community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection of women from acts of violence;
d. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
e. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, higher education institutions and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women; and
f. opening complaint posts for the protection of women from acts of violence.
Part Seven Protection in the Workplace

Part Three
Prevention and Protection Article 22 (1) The Regional Government is obligated to undertake prevention and protection efforts against violent treatment, exploitation, discrimination, maltreatment, and neglect.
(2) The implementation of prevention and protection as referred to in paragraph (1), may cooperate with educational institutions, religious institutions, mass media, professional organizations, business entities, and/or community institutions.
(3) Prevention and protection efforts as referred to in paragraph (2) are implemented by:
a. forming networks;
b. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of prevention and protection based on partnership patterns;
c. establishing a system for prevention of violence and protection of children and women;
d. disseminating Laws and Regulations related to the protection of women victims of violence;
e. providing education for victims of violence and vulnerable groups;
JDIH Kota Singkawang
f. organizing family support in the form of family parenting education, child parenting education, family mediation, and economic support;
g. increasing the capacity of protection services for women and children including institutional capacity development and enhancement of professionalism and competence of service providers;
h. increasing the ability of individuals and/or vulnerable groups to recognize risks and dangers from situations or actions that may cause violence, exploitation, maltreatment and neglect; and i. increasing the utilization of communication, information, and education media.
(4) Prevention and protection efforts as referred to in paragraph (3) are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the OPD responsible for women's empowerment and child protection.

